---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import '../styles/pages/releases.css';
---

<DocsLayout title="Release Notes" sectionLabel="Releases" activeSlug="releases">

  <section class="section">
    <span class="section-label">Changelog</span>
    <h2>Release Notes</h2>
    <p>All notable changes to VibeCrew, following <a href="https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/">Keep a Changelog</a> and <a href="https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html">Semantic Versioning</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="version-nav">
    <a href="#v1.0.0" class="latest">v1.0.0</a>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- v1.0.0                                                       -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <div class="release-section" id="v1.0.0">
    <div class="release-header">
      <span class="release-version">v1.0.0</span>
      <span class="release-date">2026-03-04</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/fabkrum/vibe-crew/releases/tag/v1.0.0" class="release-badge latest">GitHub Release</a>
    </div>

    <p class="release-summary">The first stable release of VibeCrew &mdash; a Claude Code plugin that transforms Claude Code into an autonomous vibe-coding operating system.</p>

    <div class="change-category">
      <h3><span class="change-type added">Highlights</span></h3>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Two-Tier Workflow</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Tier 1 (Project Foundation)</strong> &mdash; Sequential process creating VISION.md, design system, TDR, architecture diagrams, roadmap, and CLAUDE.md before any source code can be written</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 2 (Feature Development)</strong> &mdash; Iterative 6-phase cycle (Plan &rarr; UI Design &rarr; Code &rarr; Test &rarr; Review &rarr; Docs) for each feature</li>
        <li>Phase gate hook enforces planning before coding &mdash; no source code writes until foundation is complete</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Specialized AI Agents</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Opus agents for planning, research, code, security, and analysis &mdash; tasks where mistakes are expensive</li>
        <li>Haiku agents for fast, mechanical tasks like routing and running shell commands</li>
        <li>Sonnet agent for template-driven documentation output</li>
        <li>Worktree isolation for heavy research, review, and evaluation &mdash; keeps your main session fast</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Lifecycle Hooks</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Zero-token bash scripts enforce safety, quality gates, phase ordering, and path restrictions</li>
        <li>Quality gate runs typecheck, lint, and build on every task completion</li>
        <li>Context usage warnings at 45% and 60% to prevent slowdowns</li>
        <li>Cost guardrails with session and daily tracking against thresholds</li>
        <li>Auto-formatting of written files via PostToolUse hook</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Slash Commands</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Setup &amp; onboarding</strong> &mdash; <code>/setup</code>, <code>/new-project</code>, <code>/onboard</code>, <code>/profile</code></li>
        <li><strong>Planning</strong> &mdash; <code>/plan-features</code>, <code>/idea</code>, <code>/status</code>, <code>/sync-issues</code></li>
        <li><strong>Development</strong> &mdash; <code>/new-feature</code>, <code>/run-backlog</code>, <code>/check</code>, <code>/debug</code>, <code>/fix-issue</code></li>
        <li><strong>Testing &amp; review</strong> &mdash; <code>/review</code>, <code>/tdd</code>, <code>/e2e</code>, <code>/perf-test</code>, <code>/a11y</code></li>
        <li><strong>Quality &amp; analysis</strong> &mdash; <code>/simplify</code>, <code>/apply-simplifications</code>, <code>/reconsider</code>, <code>/replay</code>, <code>/system-review</code></li>
        <li><strong>Safety</strong> &mdash; <code>/audit</code>, <code>/heal</code>, <code>/cost</code>, <code>/undo</code></li>
        <li><strong>Session management</strong> &mdash; <code>/wrap</code>, <code>/handoff</code>, <code>/release</code>, <code>/recover-state</code></li>
        <li><strong>Gamification</strong> &mdash; <code>/achievements</code>, <code>/quiz</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>MCP Servers</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Bundled servers for library docs (Context7), browser testing (Playwright, Chrome DevTools), and more</li>
        <li>Registry of additional servers auto-discovered and injected based on TDR technology choices</li>
        <li>Conditional activation &mdash; Semgrep, Sentry, Supabase, Stripe, Vercel, and Figma enabled from TDR</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Personalization</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Multi-dimension user profiles: code literacy, autonomy, PR review style, verbosity, gamification preference, learning mode, and risk tolerance</li>
        <li>Every agent reads the profile and adapts behavior to your experience level and preferences</li>
        <li>Preset selection or guided interview via <code>/profile</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Gamification &amp; Vibe Score</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Vibe Score quality rating per session (0&ndash;130) measuring prompt efficiency, test coverage, documentation freshness, and workflow compliance</li>
        <li>XP, leveling, badges, skill trees, streaks, and challenges that reward good development habits</li>
        <li>Performance Coach proposes permanent CLAUDE.md rule mutations based on anti-pattern detection</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Status Line</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Persistent terminal status bar showing model, context usage, cost, active feature and phase, Vibe Score, and compaction count</li>
        <li>Updates after every assistant message at zero token cost</li>
        <li>Graceful degradation when dependencies are missing</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Vibe Dashboard</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Browser-based VitePress dashboard with Kanban board, score trends, achievements, and settings</li>
        <li>Architecture overview rendering Mermaid diagrams from <code>.vibecrew/architecture/*.mmd</code></li>
        <li>Live session data via atomic JSON writes from the status line script</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Design Discovery</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>3-phase interview: Product &amp; Audience Context &rarr; Visual Direction &rarr; Component Preferences</li>
        <li>Bring-your-own design system: import from CSS, Tailwind, JSON tokens, URL, Figma, or brand PDF</li>
        <li>Both paths produce identical output: <code>design-system.css</code> + <code>design-brief.md</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Safety &amp; Security</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Permission rules with allowed and denied tool patterns</li>
        <li>Dangerous command protection (rm -rf, DROP TABLE, force push)</li>
        <li>Path restriction to project root</li>
        <li>OWASP Top 10 security auditing via <code>/audit</code></li>
        <li>CI failure diagnosis and repair via <code>/heal</code> (max 3 attempts)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Cross-Session State</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><code>.vibecrew/</code> directory with JSON state files, session logs, scores, signals, locks, and handoffs</li>
        <li>Cross-session context transfer via <code>/handoff</code></li>
        <li>Cross-project telemetry with anonymized performance data for <code>/system-review</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Documentation</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Companion docs site built with Astro, self-hosted fonts, dark/light theme, and Pagefind search</li>
        <li>Setup guides, workflow walkthroughs, architecture reference, glossary, and FAQ</li>
        <li>Auto-generated docs via Doc Generator agent during <code>/wrap</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>
